Step 1: Install uv

Run the official installation script directly in your PowerShell terminal:

PowerShell
powershell -ExecutionPolicy ByPass -c "irm https://astral.sh/uv/install.ps1 | iex"
Alternative Installers:

Via WinGet: winget install --id astral-sh.uv

Via Pip: pip install uv

Step 2: Add uv to PATH (If Already Installed)

If you have already installed uv but PowerShell still cannot find it, manually append its default installation directory to your environment path:

PowerShell
$env:Path += ";$env:USERPROFILE\.cargo\bin;$env:USERPROFILE\.local\bin"
To permanently add it to your user PATH:

PowerShell
[Environment]::SetEnvironmentVariable("Path", $env:Path + ";$env:USERPROFILE\.cargo\bin", "User")
Step 3: Refresh Terminal and Verify

Fully close and restart VS Code (or open a new PowerShell window).

Verify the command works:

PowerShell
uv --version
Once it returns a version number (e.g., uv 0.x.x), re-run your initial command:

PowerShell
uv init .


uv add langchain langgraph langchain-groq python-dotenv tavily-agent-toolkit langgraph-checkpoint-postgres "psycopg[binary,pool]" langsmith